  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 144 PM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nMid-level ridging will dominate the period leading to warm and \nmostly rain free conditions outside of isolated seabreeze convection \neach day. As we approach Thursday night into Friday morning, we will \nsee a mid-level shortwave tracking along the southern periphery of \nthe ridge. This will lead to an increase in the moisture regime, \nsurging PWATs around 2.0 inches (75th percentile of climatology). \nThis shortwave will bring PVA to the area, and resulting small scale \nlift will allow for low rain chances (~20%) during the morning and \nafternoon on Friday. \n\nWill continue to monitor the need for short-fused heat related \nproducts. We could see peak heat indices of 110 to 115 with dew \npoints in the mid to upper 70s into next week. This translates to \nmoderate to extreme HeatRisk conditions. An additional risk for \nelevated fire weather exists over the Rio Grande Plains into the \nweekend due to low RH (~25%) and sustained 20mph winds gusting to \n25mph. We strongly encourage the practice of heat safety in these \nconditions. Take frequent breaks and remember to stay hydrated, \ncheck those backseats, and avoid long exposure in these \ntemperatures. For more information be sure to check out \nweather.gov/heatsafety.",
